{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"spoiled-loopy-pinemarten","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The DC harness project has NO 'Epic' issue type, so the epic-parent path cannot be tested live\n\n## Evidence\n\nHarness run **30857265932** (main @ `b301e7513d`, i.e. WITH change 1311),\n`test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link`:\n\n    SETUP FAILED (not a rebar defect): project RBJSXPQ offers no 'Epic' issue type\n    (has ['Sub-task', 'Task'])\n\n`collected=58`, 6 failed / 51 passed / 1 xfailed.\n\nThe cell reported SETUP FAILED distinctly rather than as an ambiguous red — that branch was written\nfor exactly this case — so the diagnosis cost nothing. But the consequence is real.\n\n## What this blocks\n\nThe scratch project is created from whichever template the DC image ships, and that template offers\nonly `Sub-task` and `Task`. **No Epic issue type means no Epic Link relationship can be created**,\nso on this harness:\n\n * [rebar:39c1-2a32-b564-4b4b] **AC1 cannot be arbitrated.** Change 1311's Epic Link write is\n   unexercised live — the cell cannot reach the code. This is the THIRD distinct reason that AC has\n   gone unproven (first the emit/apply gates were disjoint, then the greenhopper route 404'd, now\n   the fixture cannot build the fixture).\n * [rebar:9bb9-56a3-e9c0-46e9] **AC3 likewise** — the read side cannot be proven for the epic case\n   either, for the same reason.\n\nBoth changes are unit-proven and neither is live-proven. Given 1276, 1288 and 1302 each shipped\nmutation-proven and wrong, that is exactly the gap this epic exists to close.\n\n## Why this is a harness defect, not a product one\n\nNothing about rebar is implicated. `_seed_epic` correctly discovers the project's issue types rather\nthan hardcoding `Epic` (the same discipline `_subtask_type_name` follows), and correctly reports\nSETUP rather than blaming the transport. The gap is that the harness provisions a project which\ncannot express the relationship under test.\n\n## Candidate fixes, cheapest first — none yet verified\n\n 1. **Create the scratch project from a Jira SOFTWARE template** rather than whatever the image\n    defaults to. Epic ships with the Software templates; the Core/Business ones do not carry it.\n    `conftest.py:359` already records a prior attempt at pinning a template\n    (`com.pyxis.greenhopper.jira:gh-simplified-kanban-classic`), so the machinery and the prior art\n    both exist — check why that pin is not in force.\n 2. **Add the Epic issue type to the project's issue-type scheme** after creation, via REST.\n 3. **Provision a second project** from a Software template solely for the epic cells.\n\nOption 1 is the obvious first try given the existing comment, but the template list an image offers\nis version-specific and must be READ from the instance, not assumed — the same lesson `_seed_epic`\nalready encodes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the harness project (or a project the epic cells use) offers an `Epic` issue type, discovered\n      from the instance rather than assumed\n- [ ] `test_outbound_epic_parent_round_trips_via_the_epic_link` EXECUTES — it reaches its assertions\n      instead of reporting SETUP FAILED — on a harness run, with the run id recorded\n- [ ] whichever template or scheme change is made is discovered/verified at runtime, so a future DC\n      image that ships a different template set fails loudly rather than silently reverting to a\n      project without Epic\n- [ ] the canary line still shows `skipped` at its expected baseline — this must not be \"fixed\" by\n      skipping the cell","id":"3fe5-c22e-dc2d-4c9e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC harness project has no Epic issue type, so the epic-parent path cannot be tested live"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785797442891692001,"uuid":"660436a2-ea96-4754-b73a-b990b3f3836d"}